### Fetch data with cleanup to avoid race conditions

Source: https://react.dev/learn/you-might-not-need-an-effect

Use this Effect to fetch data based on query and page while ignoring stale responses. The cleanup function sets a flag to prevent out-of-order responses from updating state.

```jsx
function SearchResults({ query }) {
  const [results, setResults] = useState([]);
  const [page, setPage] = useState(1);
  useEffect(() => {
    let ignore = false;
    fetchResults(query, page).then(json => {
      if (!ignore) {
        setResults(json);
      }
    });
    return () => {
      ignore = true;
    };
  }, [query, page]);

  function handleNextPageClick() {
    setPage(page + 1);
  }
  // ...
}
```

