### Controlled text area with useState

Source: https://react.dev/reference/react-dom/components/textarea

Passes `value` and `onChange` to a `<textarea>` so React forces the input to match the state variable. Without `onChange`, typing would be impossible because React reverts the value after each keystroke.

```jsx
function NewPost() {
  const [postContent, setPostContent] = useState(''); // Declare a state variable...
  // ...
  return (
    <textarea
      value={postContent} // ...force the input's value to match the state variable...
      onChange={e => setPostContent(e.target.value)} // ... and update the state variable on any edits!
    />
  );
}
```

